# Test coverage artifacts (pytest-cov)
.coverage
coverage.xml
*.csv
# Small, human-editable reference tables -- the *inputs* that change what
# buem simulates, as opposed to the multi-MB extracted building tables the
# blanket *.csv rule above is aimed at. These must ship.
#
# Everything under data/reference/ is such a table by construction: that
# directory holds only the editable inputs a reviewer is expected to read
# and change. Whitelisting the directory rather than each file stops a new
# table being silently swallowed by the *.csv rule -- which is exactly
# what happened to the occupancy, glazing, envelope and setback tables
# when they were added.
!src/buem/data/reference/*.csv
!src/buem/data/buildings/netherlands/Loenen/u_value_reference.csv
!src/buem/data/buildings/netherlands/Loenen/service_building_reference.csv
!src/buem/data/buildings/netherlands/Loenen/refurbishment_measure_reference.csv
# Copied unchanged from Loenen/ -- country-level TABULA/Bouwbesluit data,
# not region-specific -- so Heeten's batch runs get the same window-U-value
# and service-building corrections rather than silently falling back to
# uncorrected TABULA values (see CHANGELOG's Heeten entry).
!src/buem/data/buildings/netherlands/Heeten/u_value_reference.csv
!src/buem/data/buildings/netherlands/Heeten/service_building_reference.csv
!src/buem/data/buildings/netherlands/Heeten/refurbishment_measure_reference.csv
!src/buem/data/reference/dhw_cooking_constants.csv
*.xlsx
!src/buem/data/default_2016.xlsx
# Demo_EN_12831-3_DHW_needs_2021-09-02.xlsx (src/buem/data/reference/) is
# deliberately NOT allowlisted here -- its EPB Center redistribution
# license hasn't been verified, same posture this repo already takes with
# occupancy's CREST workbooks (CC BY-NC-ND, also not redistributed). Kept
# locally for scripts/extract_dhw_reference_values.py to read from on a
# machine that has it; the small, clearly-attributed CSV it produces
# (allowlisted above) is what's actually committed.
*.h5
*.nc
*.parquet
*.feather
*.zip
*.tar
*.gz
*.egg-info/
src/buem/_version.py
.git/
.idea/
.vscode/
.softwares/*

# Ignoring results, caches, and run artifacts
src/buem/results/*
!src/buem/results/standard_plots.py

# Generated building JSON files (pipeline output — regenerated from data)
src/buem/data/buildings/germany/
src/buem/data/buildings/_parquet_cache/

# Documentation builds and caches
docs/build/
docs/_build/
docs/.doctrees/
*.doctree

# Sphinx temporary files
docs/source/_autosummary/

# Local conda environment (use global instead)
.conda/

# Claude Code context (CLAUDE.md, .claude/) -- local-only, not pushed to
# GitHub (2026-08-04): internal AI-agent working notes/incident log, not
# meant for external partners (EnerPlanET) browsing this repo. Previously
# tracked and already present in prior pushed commits/tags -- this only
# stops future changes from being committed, it doesn't rewrite history.
CLAUDE.md
.claude/

# LibreOffice/OpenOffice lock files -- created while a bundled CSV (e.g. the
# editable u_value_reference.csv) is open in a spreadsheet, and left behind
# on a crash. Never part of the dataset.
.~lock.*#